toolbar.description:
To leave an item out, list it with "disabled": true. To add a button, give it a name, a command and a rank: the items of Whybook are ranked 10 (epi-view: Code, Bench, Map), 20 (epi-mode: Wonder, Do, Report), 30 (epi-layout: where the panels go), 40 (epi-detail), 50 (epi-run-all), 60 (epi-ai), 100 (the spacer), 1000 (kernelName) and 1001 (kernelStatus). Whybook's commands act on its view, such as whybook:interrupt-kernel, whybook:restart-kernel, whybook:run-all-cells and docmanager:save; the commands of the buttons of JupyterLab's notebook toolbar act on that view only. For example:
{
  "toolbar": [
    { "name": "epi-mode", "disabled": true },
    { "name": "interrupt", "command": "whybook:interrupt-kernel", "rank": 55 },
    { "name": "restart", "command": "whybook:restart-kernel", "rank": 56 }
  ]
}
